# CSS structure (no arbitrary inline CSS)

## Default

- **Layout, spacing, typography, colors:** use **Tailwind** classes in JSX (`className`) and/or **`cn()`** when merging.
- **Component-specific or repeated visual rules** (especially Wysteria / archive admin / v2 shell): put them in a **colocated `*.css` file** next to the component (or in `components/wl-home-v2/wl-home-v2.css` for shared shell tokens) and **import** it from the TSX file (`import "./feature.css"`).
- **Class naming:** follow existing prefixes (`wl-home-v2-*`, feature-specific blocks) so styles stay grep-able and consistent with `wl-home-v2.css`.

## Avoid

- **`style={{ … }}`** for static or design-token styling — move to Tailwind or the colocated stylesheet.
- Large style objects or one-off inline styles that belong in CSS for readability and theming.

## Exceptions (inline `style` is OK)

- **Truly dynamic values** only available at runtime (e.g. width/height from measurement, drag position, chart geometry).
- Setting a **single CSS variable** on a wrapper for use inside nested CSS (e.g. `--progress: 0.5`) when the value is computed in JS.

When touching **shadcn / Radix** primitives, prefer **Tailwind + `className`** overrides; use `style` only when the library or behavior requires it.
